 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity**: $O(N)$, where $N = W \times H$. The operations (grid generation, matrix multiplication, normalization) are vectorizable and parallelizable across pixels.
-*   **Memory Complexity**: $O(N)$ to store origins and directions.
-*   **Performance**: Highly efficient on GPUs due to tensor operations. The bottleneck is typically the matrix inversion if done per-frame (though $VP$ is usually constant per camera pose) or the unprojection API call overhead.
-*   **Strengths**: Generalizable to any camera model supported by the unprojection API; handles arbitrary extrinsics and intrinsics.
-*   **Limitations**: Requires accurate camera calibration. If the inverse matrix is singular (e.g., camera at infinity), it fails. Precision issues may arise with very large or very small scene scales if not using double precision for the matrix inversion [S1, unofficial].
